        <argsstring>(QRQueryProgressFunc func, void *arg)</argsstring>
        <name>setProgressFunc</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classqrs_1_1QRQueryOperator_1ab6aa9c9883ae0d1a05d1d132db1dd14f" kindref="member">QRQueryProgressFunc</ref></type>
          <declname>func</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>void *</type>
          <declname>arg</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Sets progress event-handler. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The event handler(<emphasis>func</emphasis>) supplied is of type QRQueryProgressFunc, which contains three arguments: <emphasis>isInit</emphasis> (boolean), <emphasis>count(unsigned)</emphasis> and a user-supplied argument (<emphasis>arg</emphasis>). This event-handler is called first with <emphasis>isInit</emphasis> set to &apos;true&apos; and <emphasis>count</emphasis> with the total number of domain elements. Afterwards, the event-handler is called for every node queried with <emphasis>isInit</emphasis> set to &apos;false&apos; and <emphasis>count</emphasis> set to the number of nodes queried at that point. </para>        </detaileddescription>
